// The position map: parameters and locals of the function being canonicalised,
// in the order they were first met. A name is answered with its position, so
// renaming every variable in a function cannot change its fingerprint, while
// using one name where another function used two still can.
//
// Only names of the function's own variables ever reach here. Called
// functions, imported globals and exported names are kept verbatim by their
// callers, which is what lets two otherwise identical functions differ by
// which name they mention.

cn(string name) {
  int idx = find_str((import cnames), name);
  if(idx < 0) {
    idx = cn_add(name);
  }
  string ret_s = "" + idx;
} return string ret_s;

cn_add(string name) {
  push((import cnames), name);
  int ret_i = len((import cnames)) - 1;
} return int ret_i;
